# Codex permission rules. Tracked deliberately: an untracked allow-list is per-machine, so
# two operators get different agent behaviour from the same task.
# Read-only and hermetic only. Mutating and irreversible commands are deliberately absent --
# they fall through to a prompt, which is the decision point.
# Added 2026-08-31.
# DELIBERATELY BROAD, and the reason matters.
# bd update --notes overwrites and once silently blanked a bead (fddc771).
# It CANNOT be expressed here: prefix patterns are positional literals with alternation and no
# wildcard, and `bd update <id> --notes` puts the bead ID between the two tokens. Narrowing to
# specific verbs would make every --claim/--status/--append-notes prompt, which agents do
# constantly. The correct mechanism reads full argv: a bd-notes-guard PreToolUse hook.
prefix_rule(pattern=["bd"], decision="allow")
